  "notes": "A する verb composed of {停|てい} (stop) + {止|し} (cease). A formal, written-style word for stopping or halting. Both transitive (to stop something) and intransitive (something stops) uses are common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {一時|いちじ}{停止|ていし}: temporary stop/pause\n- {運転|うんてん}{停止|ていし}: shutdown (of a machine/plant)\n- {免許|めんきょ}{停止|ていし}: license suspension\n- {活動|かつどう}を{停止|ていし}する: to cease activities\n- {緊急|きんきゅう}{停止|ていし}: emergency stop\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {止|と}まる / {止|と}める: to stop — everyday equivalent; less formal\n- {中止|ちゅうし}する: to cancel, to call off — stopping something planned before or during execution\n- {中断|ちゅうだん}する: to interrupt, to break off — implies temporary interruption with possible resumption",
  "conjugation_type": "suru",
